This is a textbook case of **coverage-gaming tests** — every production method is called (→ 95%+ line coverage) but almost nothing meaningful is asserted. Here's the severity-ranked audit:

---

## 🔴 CRITICAL — Missing assertions (tests prove nothing)

### 1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)
**Anti-pattern:** Fire-and-forget — no assert at all.
Calls `AddProduct` but never checks the product was persisted.
```csharp
// Fix: verify the product is retrievable after adding
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var saved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(saved);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", saved.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, saved.Price);
```

### 2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)
**Anti-pattern:** Fire-and-forget — calls `UpdatePrice`, never checks the price changed.
A bug where `Save` is called with the *old* price would pass this test.
```csharp
// Fix: assert the new price
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

### 3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)
**Anti-pattern:** Fire-and-forget — calls `RemoveProduct`, never checks it was deleted.
```csharp
// Fix: assert the product is gone
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

### 4. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)
**Anti-pattern:** Fire-and-forget — doesn't even capture the return value meaningfully, and tests on an *empty* catalog so it exercises the least interesting path.
```csharp
// Fix: assert count reflects actual state
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-002", "Gadget", 19.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(2, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

### 5. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)
**Anti-pattern:** Fire-and-forget — applies a 10% discount but never checks any price changed. A no-op implementation would pass.
```csharp
// Fix: assert discounted prices
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

### 6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 84)
**Anti-pattern:** Fire-and-forget — imports CSV but never checks any products exist.
```csharp
